course: dictionary
lesson: 14581
title: Placental mammals
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Placental is a science word. It describes things to do with the placenta, the organ that grows inside a mother during pregnancy. The placenta gives the baby food and oxygen while it grows.
explain: Some animals are called placental mammals. Their babies grow inside the mother with a placenta. «Humans, dogs, cats and whales are placental mammals.» Most mammals are placental.
explain: Scientists compare them with other mammals. Kangaroos and koalas are marsupials, because their babies grow in a pouch. The platypus is a monotreme, because it lays eggs. Each group grows its young in a different way.
explain: To check the meaning in context, look for clues. If the sentence talks about a mother, a growing baby, and food or oxygen passing to it, the word placental fits. Swap in your meaning to see if it still makes sense.
fact: The placenta is an organ that grows inside a mother during pregnancy.
fact: The placenta gives the baby food and oxygen.
fact: «Placental» means to do with the placenta, or having babies that grow inside the mother with one.
fact: Placental mammals include humans, dogs, cats and whales.
fact: Most mammals are placental, while kangaroos and koalas are marsupials and the platypus is a monotreme.
exercise: «Dogs and cats are placental mammals.» What does placental describe? | *Mammals whose babies grow inside the mother | Fish that swim in the sea | Animals whose babies grow in a pouch | Animals that lay eggs
exercise: The placenta gives the baby food and oxygen. What is the placenta? | A type of egg | *An organ inside a mother that feeds the baby during pregnancy | A kind of kangaroo | A pouch on the outside of the mother
exercise: «Kangaroos and koalas are marsupials, but humans are placental.» Find and copy the word that means animals whose babies grow in a pouch. | *marsupials | placental | humans | mammals
test: «Whales are placental mammals, so their babies grow inside the mother.» Which animal is a marsupial? | *Koala | Whale | Cat | Dog
test: «The platypus lays eggs, so it is not a placental mammal.» Why is the platypus not placental? | It is too small | *Its babies do not grow inside the mother with a placenta | It has fur | It swims in water
exam: «Scientists sort mammals into placental, marsupial and monotreme groups.» Which group do kangaroos belong to? | Reptile | Monotreme | Placental | *Marsupial
